1307
00:54:35.653 --> 00:54:37.203
Because it's an important one,

1308
00:54:38.680 --> 00:54:40.710
especially when there is a lot of suffering in the world

1309
00:54:40.710 --> 00:54:41.543
and people think,

1310
00:54:41.543 --> 00:54:45.203
oh, I shouldn't be having a joyful goal to go,

1311
00:54:46.950 --> 00:54:49.543
summit X peaks and how, what a nice life I have.

1312
00:54:49.543 --> 00:54:51.033
Like I shouldn't,

1313
00:54:51.033 --> 00:54:52.310
I mean, these are conversation I hear all the time.

1314
00:54:52.310 --> 00:54:55.070
And it's a real conversation.

1315
00:54:55.070 --> 00:54:58.070
In our family tree of words that are cousins and siblings,

1316
00:54:59.640 --> 00:55:04.640
I feel like we are putting a challenge and pain and grit

1317
00:55:05.440 --> 00:55:07.070
and all those things that you're talking about,

1318
00:55:07.070 --> 00:55:11.240
hard, really, really close to the word integrity.

1319
00:55:11.240 --> 00:55:12.690
Because you're basically saying

1320
00:55:12.690 --> 00:55:14.650
that if you don't have all those things,

1321
00:55:14.650 --> 00:55:16.673
then you're not like trying your best

1322
00:55:16.673 --> 00:55:17.900
and you don't have integrity.

1323
00:55:17.900 --> 00:55:20.540
And maybe we should talk about integrity

1324
00:55:20.540 --> 00:55:22.370
if maybe that's not even the right word

1325
00:55:22.370 --> 00:55:24.820
should be closer to joy

1326
00:55:24.820 --> 00:55:28.290
and can joy be closer related to integrity.

1327
00:55:28.290 --> 00:55:31.520
Does that feel like the judgment,

1328
00:55:31.520 --> 00:55:32.810
the note beneath the note,

1329
00:55:32.810 --> 00:55:34.380
like what's the judgment on a person

1330
00:55:34.380 --> 00:55:36.150
who's not gritting like that?

1331
00:55:36.150 --> 00:55:38.820
Is it that that they're a bad person.

1332
00:55:38.820 --> 00:55:41.160
I think it goes back to

1333
00:55:41.160 --> 00:55:42.630
what you were saying at the beginning too,

1334
00:55:42.630 --> 00:55:44.960
what do they believe to be true about themselves

1335
00:55:44.960 --> 00:55:46.180
to begin with?

1336
00:55:46.180 --> 00:55:48.680
'Cause I think that's why people don't access joy.

1337
00:55:49.697 --> 00:55:51.560
'Cause you're saying what does being joyful

1338
00:55:51.560 --> 00:55:54.100
and chasing joy say about me.

1339
00:55:54.100 --> 00:55:56.802
Yeah. Like I don't work hard enough.

1340
00:55:56.802 --> 00:55:57.670
It shouldn't come easily to me.

1341
00:55:57.670 --> 00:55:58.970
You're a trivial person

1342
00:56:00.251 --> 00:56:01.910
'cause you're not exerting enough grit.

1343
00:56:01.910 --> 00:56:04.740
And if you're perhaps not that joyful,

1344
00:56:04.740 --> 00:56:09.200
but not working that hard, then you're a weak person.

1345
00:56:09.200 --> 00:56:12.140
And I'm not saying don't, I'm all for joy over here.

1346
00:56:12.140 --> 00:56:13.957
I think it's an important thing.

1347
00:56:13.957 --> 00:56:17.080
And it's just a conversation I've heard

1348
00:56:17.080 --> 00:56:21.260
more often than I would have expected over the past year,

1349
00:56:21.260 --> 00:56:23.910
which begs many different questions.

1350
00:56:23.910 --> 00:56:25.039
What you're saying is,

1351
00:56:25.039 --> 00:56:28.520
what you're hearing is that it would be indulgent of me

1352
00:56:28.520 --> 00:56:30.950
to pursue something that brings me joy

1353
00:56:30.950 --> 00:56:34.030
in this moment of difficulty for everybody

1354
00:56:34.030 --> 00:56:37.400
and I don't feel deserving of that.

1355
00:56:37.400 --> 00:56:38.233
Or what does that even feel like?

1356
00:56:38.233 --> 00:56:39.230
I think that's different though,

1357
00:56:39.230 --> 00:56:42.010
that's a different avenue of that

1358
00:56:42.010 --> 00:56:46.085
than the I'm not working hard enough if I'm not suffering.

1359
00:56:46.085 --> 00:56:47.078
Yeah, those are different things.

1360
00:56:47.078 --> 00:56:49.060
I think that those are two different things.

1361
00:56:49.060 --> 00:56:52.170
I think the first one does tie into the values again,

1362
00:56:52.170 --> 00:56:53.370
and what's important to me,

1363
00:56:53.370 --> 00:56:58.370
and it's okay that I go further myself despite these times,

1364
00:56:59.200 --> 00:57:00.400
because guess what,

1365
00:57:00.400 --> 00:57:03.710
when I come back from that call to adventure,

1366
00:57:03.710 --> 00:57:06.240
as Joseph Campbell says with the elixir

1367
00:57:06.240 --> 00:57:09.830
and I can contribute more energy and love and joy

1368
00:57:09.830 --> 00:57:12.210
to my community and bring that wisdom

1369
00:57:12.210 --> 00:57:16.580
and that growth with me and try in my best way

1370
00:57:16.580 --> 00:57:18.790
to to disseminate that.

1371
00:57:18.790 --> 00:57:22.830
I think that's a bigger contribution overall

1372
00:57:22.830 --> 00:57:27.163
than worrying in the moment what others might think of me.

1373
00:57:28.550 --> 00:57:31.040
That's a bigger question that we're running into right now

1374
00:57:31.040 --> 00:57:32.240
with regards to mental health.

1375
00:57:32.240 --> 00:57:34.630
Like I need to take care of myself

1376
00:57:34.630 --> 00:57:38.040
and if that is something that I wanna follow through on

1377
00:57:38.040 --> 00:57:41.270
and brings me joy, or even just that I feel drawn to,

1378
00:57:41.270 --> 00:57:44.210
or there's a curiosity pulling me towards that,

1379
00:57:44.210 --> 00:57:47.473
that is a nugget that we should pursue.

1380
00:57:49.180 --> 00:57:50.710
I almost feel like crying

1381
00:57:50.710 --> 00:57:53.240
because in the last couple of weeks,

1382
00:57:53.240 --> 00:57:57.690
I feel like I've aligned myself with more brands.

1383
00:57:57.690 --> 00:58:00.010
I'm still a sponsored athlete

1384
00:58:00.010 --> 00:58:02.490
and I have aligned myself with brands

1385
00:58:02.490 --> 00:58:06.410
that have actually embraced me as a whole person

1386
00:58:06.410 --> 00:58:09.820
and it's made me realize how much before that

1387
00:58:09.820 --> 00:58:12.218
I felt like I had to be what you said,

1388
00:58:12.218 --> 00:58:15.580
this like furrowed brow person.

1389
00:58:15.580 --> 00:58:18.180
And I would segment off all the parts of my life

1390
00:58:18.180 --> 00:58:19.250
from each other

1391
00:58:19.250 --> 00:58:22.020
so that I appeared to be doing

1392
00:58:22.020 --> 00:58:23.960
what everybody wanted me to do in those worlds.

1393
00:58:23.960 --> 00:58:25.170
And it was a really hard,

1394
00:58:25.170 --> 00:58:28.320
I felt like an octopus ride, like eight legs

1395
00:58:28.320 --> 00:58:29.580
and they were all in different directions

1396
00:58:29.580 --> 00:58:31.970
and they couldn't touch each other.

1397
00:58:31.970 --> 00:58:35.080
And last week I finally I saw you Rich in Texas,

1398
00:58:35.080 --> 00:58:38.100
but I finally got to spend time with a team mate

1399
00:58:38.100 --> 00:58:41.240
just joined that, it actually really does embrace me

1400
00:58:41.240 --> 00:58:44.130
for the whole thing and that joy was okay.

1401
00:58:44.130 --> 00:58:46.770
And I feel so embarrassed to like,

1402
00:58:46.770 --> 00:58:48.573
say that it took me a really long time

1403
00:58:48.573 --> 00:58:50.840
to feel like that was okay.

1404
00:58:50.840 --> 00:58:53.800
And now I feel like after New York,

1405
00:58:53.800 --> 00:58:56.150
I got so many messages of people who were like,

1406
00:58:56.150 --> 00:58:57.378
I'm gonna run a race and smile.

1407
00:58:57.378 --> 00:58:59.240
And I was like, almost cried

1408
00:58:59.240 --> 00:59:01.537
because why couldn't they do that before?

1409
00:59:01.537 --> 00:59:04.400
And why did they have to see me do that

1410
00:59:04.400 --> 00:59:07.930
in order for them to feel like they could enjoy a race

1411
00:59:07.930 --> 00:59:09.729
or like dance or something.

1412
00:59:09.729 --> 00:59:13.260
And so I just feel like my whole life is changing now

1413
00:59:13.260 --> 00:59:14.964
and I wanna be more joyful

1414
00:59:14.964 --> 00:59:17.780
and that I'm not hurting anybody by being joyful.

1415
00:59:17.780 --> 00:59:19.980
And I think all we want is to not hurt people

1416
00:59:19.980 --> 00:59:21.640
or disappoint them.

1417
00:59:21.640 --> 00:59:23.450
Like I even told you Rich that I felt

1418
00:59:23.450 --> 00:59:26.750
I didn't wanna disappoint you because I drank.

1419
00:59:26.750 --> 00:59:28.538
And that was a really hard thing to tell you.

1420
00:59:28.538 --> 00:59:30.730
I don't know why I'm feeling this here like this.

1421
00:59:30.730 --> 00:59:32.090
It's real though.

1422
00:59:32.090 --> 00:59:34.030
What you're saying is extremely real.

1423
00:59:34.030 --> 00:59:38.800
I think maybe our experience as a woman

1424
00:59:38.800 --> 00:59:40.300
can be different trying to please

1425
00:59:40.300 --> 00:59:41.890
and have that feeling as an athlete.

1426
00:59:41.890 --> 00:59:44.780
Like I have to make, make sure everybody approves of me.

1427
00:59:44.780 --> 00:59:47.910
I don't know, I'm not in y'all shoes so I don't know.

1428
00:59:47.910 --> 00:59:49.550
I mean, certainly that burden is heavier-

1429
00:59:49.550 --> 00:59:51.080
It's heavy.
If you're a female athlete.

1430
00:59:51.080 --> 00:59:53.820
I think it can be heavy in maybe a different way.

1431
00:59:53.820 --> 00:59:55.050
I'm only speaking for myself,

1432
00:59:55.050 --> 00:59:56.070
I can't speak for everybody else,

1433
00:59:56.070 --> 00:59:57.870
but I think that does tie

1434
00:59:57.870 --> 01:00:00.500
into everything we're talking about.

1435
01:00:00.500 --> 01:00:03.690
Because when we sit here and have this feeling of,

1436
01:00:03.690 --> 01:00:05.840
I need to do these things.

1437
01:00:05.840 --> 01:00:07.040
It's like, for who?

1438
01:00:07.040 --> 01:00:08.160
Again, who are you becoming?

1439
01:00:08.160 --> 01:00:10.120
For who, what are we doing this?

1440
01:00:10.120 --> 01:00:12.270
I think it's beautiful what you said, Alexi.

1441
01:00:12.270 --> 01:00:15.410
But that also ties into what we were saying earlier.

1442
01:00:15.410 --> 01:00:18.330
Like if you're other parts of you,

1443
01:00:18.330 --> 01:00:20.470
your eight legs aren't integrated

1444
01:00:20.470 --> 01:00:23.740
towards the values and principles of you,

1445
01:00:23.740 --> 01:00:26.450
truly, you, then it feels like that.

1446
01:00:26.450 --> 01:00:29.456
And when it all comes together,

1447
01:00:29.456 --> 01:00:30.910
it doesn't have to be in perfect alignment,

1448
01:00:30.910 --> 01:00:34.213
but they're all sort of working towards the same north star,

1449
01:00:34.213 --> 01:00:38.210
your energy and love and joy and passion

1450
01:00:38.210 --> 01:00:42.430
and what you exude is 10 times more powerful.

1451
01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:45.660
And people feel that, they feel that.

1452
01:00:45.660 --> 01:00:46.980
You have let go,

1453
01:00:46.980 --> 01:00:51.050
your lighter and you exude an energy and a joy

1454
01:00:51.050 --> 01:00:53.840
because you are getting more and more in alignment

1455
01:00:55.520 --> 01:00:58.060
towards that higher self of you

1456
01:00:58.060 --> 01:01:00.560
and the energy that you were scattering

1457
01:01:00.560 --> 01:01:02.653
amongst those eight legs.

1458
01:01:03.860 --> 01:01:07.170
Before it was still amazing energy

1459
01:01:07.170 --> 01:01:11.350
but now it's all coming together into one energy packet

1460
01:01:11.350 --> 01:01:13.260
and that's gonna,

1461
01:01:13.260 --> 01:01:16.380
it took me 25 years to figure this out.

1462
01:01:16.380 --> 01:01:18.230
The fact that you're figuring it out now.

1463
01:01:18.230 --> 01:01:20.300
And I think it goes in ebbs and flows too.

1464
01:01:20.300 --> 01:01:22.160
I know there's been times in my life

1465
01:01:22.160 --> 01:01:25.080
where I wouldn't have ever questioned joy.

1466
01:01:25.080 --> 01:01:26.250
And then other times where I'm like,

1467
01:01:26.250 --> 01:01:28.370
wait, no, I can't possibly have fun.

1468
01:01:28.370 --> 01:01:31.030
Or like, I can't possibly do this and enjoy,

1469
01:01:31.030 --> 01:01:33.630
I need to like stay here and focus and do the,

1470
01:01:33.630 --> 01:01:37.620
and it robs the joy like ironically,

1471
01:01:37.620 --> 01:01:40.170
everything is taken from that experience.

1472
01:01:40.170 --> 01:01:42.070
And I don't even have the same experience

1473
01:01:42.070 --> 01:01:43.713
and then I end up not even doing

1474
01:01:43.713 --> 01:01:45.413
the thing that I wanted to do

1475
01:01:45.413 --> 01:01:48.240
because there was no joy attached to any of it.

1476
01:01:48.240 --> 01:01:49.693
Being overly regimented.

1477
01:01:51.120 --> 01:01:52.270
And it's right there.

1478
01:01:53.497 --> 01:01:55.800
That's immersing verses attending

1479
01:01:55.800 --> 01:01:58.370
because when we showed up with that furrowed brow

1480
01:01:58.370 --> 01:01:59.343
because we had to.

1481
01:02:00.329 --> 01:02:02.500
Because we told ourselves with a past story,

1482
01:02:02.500 --> 01:02:05.600
well, this is just who we are, what we need to do now.

1483
01:02:05.600 --> 01:02:07.480
Someone told us that, or our society

1484
01:02:07.480 --> 01:02:08.650
or whomever, whatever.

1485
01:02:08.650 --> 01:02:10.180
And that's what we are told.

1486
01:02:10.180 --> 01:02:14.230
Whereas you don't tell a writer or an artist or a musician

1487
01:02:14.230 --> 01:02:17.430
to just show up, they show up with this energy

1488
01:02:17.430 --> 01:02:20.160
and this passion and this depth

1489
01:02:20.160 --> 01:02:21.920
that if I'm going to do it,

1490
01:02:21.920 --> 01:02:25.050
I'm gonna show up with all myself.

1491
01:02:25.050 --> 01:02:28.450
And they bring this totally different energy to it

1492
01:02:28.450 --> 01:02:31.750
and it's immersing versus attending, what I say.

1493
01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:33.740
You're immersing yourself in the moment

1494
01:02:33.740 --> 01:02:35.050
versus just attending.

1495
01:02:35.050 --> 01:02:37.530
I love, I'm gonna write on the whiteboard.

1496
01:02:37.530 --> 01:02:41.040
It's also allowing versus forcing.

1497
01:02:41.040 --> 01:02:44.420
Like if you contrast that athlete mentality

1498
01:02:44.420 --> 01:02:46.770
of like willfulness and I'm gonna make it happen

1499
01:02:46.770 --> 01:02:48.324
and I'm holding on so tightly

1500
01:02:48.324 --> 01:02:51.460
versus a more creative pursuit,

1501
01:02:51.460 --> 01:02:53.350
like if you watch the Beatles documentary,

1502
01:02:53.350 --> 01:02:55.327
like they're hanging out,

1503
01:02:55.327 --> 01:02:57.240
and a lot of it is fucking around

1504
01:02:57.240 --> 01:03:00.160
and that's because you need that

1505
01:03:00.160 --> 01:03:05.160
in order to create the space for the little spark to arise.

1506
01:03:05.390 --> 01:03:08.120
You have to hold it loosely

1507
01:03:08.120 --> 01:03:10.120
in order for the magic to occur.

1508
01:03:10.120 --> 01:03:14.000
And you can't be like strict on your timetable

1509
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:15.490
or your agenda.

1510
01:03:15.490 --> 01:03:16.870
And I think there's something to be said

1511
01:03:16.870 --> 01:03:19.630
for approaching your athletic pursuits

1512
01:03:19.630 --> 01:03:22.190
or other pursuits in your life with that sensibility.

1513
01:03:22.190 --> 01:03:25.770
And I think endurance provides you with those quiet moments.

1514
01:03:25.770 --> 01:03:26.603
Like, 'cause you're out,

1515
01:03:26.603 --> 01:03:29.540
you can't be multitasking when you're out by yourself

1516
01:03:29.540 --> 01:03:32.250
on a trail or whatever, like you're just left with yourself.

1517
01:03:32.250 --> 01:03:34.850
So it's built in to that practice.

1518
01:03:34.850 --> 01:03:36.530
But if you're trying to get into grad school

1519
01:03:36.530 --> 01:03:38.870
or whatever it is that you're pursuing,

1520
01:03:38.870 --> 01:03:42.830
like understanding that the best ideas come

1521
01:03:42.830 --> 01:03:44.990
in the most unlikely moments,

1522
01:03:44.990 --> 01:03:46.630
they don't come when you're sitting down

1523
01:03:46.630 --> 01:03:47.980
and like forcing them to happen.

1524
01:03:47.980 --> 01:03:49.290
Holding on to tight.

1525
01:03:49.290 --> 01:03:50.470
I'm reading this book right now

1526
01:03:50.470 --> 01:03:53.270
and I circled a couple paragraphs,

1527
01:03:53.270 --> 01:03:57.110
but it was all about how you have to look out the window

1528
01:03:57.110 --> 01:03:59.890
for at least 20 minutes a day with zero agenda.

1529
01:03:59.890 --> 01:04:01.470
Just look out the window.

1530
01:04:01.470 --> 01:04:02.490
It's like window gazing.

1531
01:04:02.490 --> 01:04:07.160
But the whole point of that is to do something mindless

1532
01:04:07.160 --> 01:04:10.690
and joyful that isn't productive

1533
01:04:10.690 --> 01:04:12.600
for you to be able to then be productive.

1534
01:04:12.600 --> 01:04:14.300
And I know it's it's we hear it all the time.

1535
01:04:14.300 --> 01:04:15.420
Like just do something,

1536
01:04:15.420 --> 01:04:17.060
not productive to them be productive,

1537
01:04:17.060 --> 01:04:18.741
but it's the same thing with sports.

1538
01:04:18.741 --> 01:04:21.383
My best race is my best performances

1539
01:04:21.383 --> 01:04:24.240
were when I was laughing behind the blocks

1540
01:04:24.240 --> 01:04:28.820
and enjoying myself and with my peers and on a relay

1541
01:04:28.820 --> 01:04:32.750
or doing, almost missing my race as a 15 year old

1542
01:04:32.750 --> 01:04:36.170
because I'm having so much fun in the moment

1543
01:04:36.170 --> 01:04:37.617
in that joyous state.

1544
01:04:37.617 --> 01:04:38.780
And I think that, yes,

1545
01:04:38.780 --> 01:04:40.760
I don't need to be missing races and doing whatever.

1546
01:04:40.760 --> 01:04:43.640
But the point is is that you can lose yourself

1547
01:04:43.640 --> 01:04:45.690
in that experience to really then

1548
01:04:45.690 --> 01:04:50.690
be able to catapult yourself for the goal that you want.

1549
01:04:51.060 --> 01:04:51.893
Well, it goes back,

1550
01:04:51.893 --> 01:04:53.447
sorry, you were gonna say something?

1551
01:04:53.447 --> 01:04:54.950
No, I can speak after you.

1552
01:04:54.950 --> 01:04:57.300
I always wanna hear what you have to say.

1553
01:04:57.300 --> 01:04:59.200
It goes back to the alter ego thing.

1554
01:05:00.610 --> 01:05:01.807
You're having fun and cracking up

1555
01:05:01.807 --> 01:05:03.170
and you have your best race

1556
01:05:03.170 --> 01:05:06.180
because you're being who you really are in that moment.

1557
01:05:06.180 --> 01:05:08.370
And I think we have this idea of like

1558
01:05:08.370 --> 01:05:10.580
when I'm training, I'm the Ironman guy.

1559
01:05:10.580 --> 01:05:12.180
And then I go to work and I'm the work guy

1560
01:05:12.180 --> 01:05:14.810
and I go home and I'm the dad and the partner.

1561
01:05:14.810 --> 01:05:19.020
And you're toggling between all these different identities

1562
01:05:19.020 --> 01:05:22.000
